Where you get a near-complete turnover of species across the treatments a=
nd=20
the number of detections in one or more treatments is very low (e.g. 11,=20=

versus 170-odd in another), I assume that the output from Distance for bo=
th=20
tests is still valid (though imprecise in one) and that you can still run=
 a Z-test=20
(as described in the manual). Where my data is like this, in many instanc=
es the=20

